Particle–substrate interactions — Don Rimai, edited by Goodarz Ahmadi (@cm-rimai-source: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cm-sources) { r_67MEFYZ26RD2ERAEKSVC0ACCQM
Don Rimai, *Particle-Substrate Interactions: Microscopic Aspects of Adhesion*, edited for course presentation by Goodarz Ahmadi, Clarkson ME437/537. [Part 1, twelve pages](https://sites.clarkson.edu/gahmadi/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2020/06/ME537-Rimai_1.pdf) · [Part 2, eleven pages](https://sites.clarkson.edu/gahmadi/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2020/06/ME537-Rimai_2.pdf). Undated notes; the upload directory is not an edition date.

Read both parts, then follow their original studies for a chosen contact system. They connect contact deformation, adhesion models, electrical interactions and measurement methods. Their numerical examples concern specified materials and geometries rather than a universal contamination-removal rule. The bibliography includes books whose availability and rights are separate from these notes.

Title, model assumptions, JKR equation, electrical examples and measurement-method passages were inspected on 30 October 2026; part 1 page 7 was also viewed visually. Not every micrograph, plotted point or cited experiment was independently checked. No blanket reuse licence was verified. Read from the institutional links and preserve both author and editor attribution; no source media is bundled.

